you know, whether it's smaller, big on that

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.320
side of the spectrum.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.360
But do you think they would ever be.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.500
I don't know.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.710
Like I don't see it ever going away.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.670
But do you think it'll come back?

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:24.860
Like, do you think, for example, of Christian
nationalism then it'll truly grow to be popular?

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:25.860
Or will it always?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.299
They're kind of this smaller niche.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:33.329
Speaker 1: I don't think any prediction I
could make about that would be worth a penny.

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:37.950
I mean, really, humans are so terrible at
making these types of predictions.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.729
And this is why when Trump was using the line
during his 2012, I think it was in 2020, he

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:45.710
would say, we will never be a socialist country.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.710
Maybe we will.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:47.710
I don't know.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.830
I mean, it doesn't seem to be going in that
direction right now.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:55.610
But how can we say the U.S. will never be
a socialist country, 500 years, a thousand

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.560
years if the U.S. is still around?

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.420
Maybe it will be a socialist country.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.700
That being said, right now there's no socialists
in power, so it's not going to happen any

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.700
time soon.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.450
So I would be very hesitant to make any.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:13.460
Maybe Christian nationalism will maybe we
will be a fully legal Christian theocracy

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.990
at some point in time.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:15.990
I don't know.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:19.030
I would hesitate to make any of these never
predictions.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.040
Speaker 2: Yeah.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.750
No, I feel that I mean, this is kind of a
what about ism?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:32.080
And I was just thinking about it because you
see, a lot of people say that Christian nationalism

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.080
is a threat.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:39.269
So I wonder, like, is it a threat in so far
as it could become popular or is it just a

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:43.250
threat insofar as this small group of people
can be very dangerous?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.989
Speaker 1: I think it depends on who you ask
and exactly where and what year it is.

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:53.430
But I think it's fair to say that Christian
nationalism is a threat in the sense that

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:57.780
it threatens the America that the founding
fathers created.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.680
That's it's a threat in that sense.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.900
And then is it a practical and imminent threat?

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:09.920
Well, there is a group that, if they took
power, would make Christian theocracy a reality.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.170
Right now, they thankfully don't have that
power, but they are certainly a threat in

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.500
that they want more power.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.930
So it's just about better defining what we
mean by threat, if that makes sense.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.780
Speaker 2: No.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.580
Yeah, that does make sense.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.580
Yeah.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:30.470
I just want to hear what your thoughts were
on that to appreciate it again.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.900
